{"format":"kards-original-reference","version":1,"id":"2cee5c6e9c28b86e","name":"card_unit_252nd_RIFLES","package":"/Game/Blueprints/Cards/Soviet/WinterWar/units/card_unit_252nd_RIFLES","parent":"UBaseCardObject","card":{"title":"252nd RIFLES","text":"Gains +1 attack when your HQ takes damage, then becomes Veteran if attack is 6+.","flavorText":"The 252nd Rifle Regiment was a unit of the 70th Rifle Division of the Red Army during the Winter War and WWII. It was initially established in 1934 at Samara but was later moved to the Leningrad Military District. The division participated in the Winter War and received the Order of Lenin for its role in breaching the Mannerheim Line. With the outbreak of Operation Barbarossa in 1941, the division relocated and engaged in counter attacks against the German invasion at Soltsy and later defending the Neva line during the Siege of Leningrad. After capturing the Nevsky Pyatachok bridgehead in the Sinyavino Offensive in 1942, the division was re-designated as the 45th Guards Rifle Division. It was reformed in April 1942 from the 47th and 146th Rifle Brigades, and engaged in battles such as the Battle of Smolensk and the advance into eastern Belarus. It played a significant role in Operation Bagration where it broke through German defenses and advanced towards the Baltic in the Riga Offensive. The 70th Division participated in battles in East Prussia, including the Battle of Memel, the Battle of Königsberg and the Samland Offensive until the end of WWII. Postwar, it undertook garrison duties in Pomerania before its disbandment in early 1947.","faction":"Soviet","type":"infantry","rarity":"Uncommon","cost":3,"operationCost":1,"attack":2,"defense":6},"defaults":{"UberGraphFrame":{},"Name":"card_unit_252nd_RIFLES","title":{"Namespace":"card_soviet","Key":"card_unit_252nd_RIFLES_title","SourceString":"252nd RIFLES","LocalizedString":"252nd RIFLES"},"Type":"ETypeEnum::infantry","attack":2,"defense":6,"range":1,"faction":"EFactionEnum::Soviet","kredits":3,"Text":{"Namespace":"card_soviet","Key":"card_unit_252nd_RIFLES_text","SourceString":"Gains +1 attack when your HQ takes damage, then becomes Veteran if attack is 6+.","LocalizedString":"Gains +1 attack when your HQ takes damage, then becomes Veteran if attack is 6+."},"flavorText":{"Namespace":"card_soviet","Key":"card_unit_252nd_RIFLES_history","SourceString":"The 252nd Rifle Regiment was a unit of the 70th Rifle Division of the Red Army during the Winter War and WWII. It was initially established in 1934 at Samara but was later moved to the Leningrad Military District. The division participated in the Winter War and received the Order of Lenin for its role in breaching the Mannerheim Line. With the outbreak of Operation Barbarossa in 1941, the division relocated and engaged in counter attacks against the German invasion at Soltsy and later defending the Neva line during the Siege of Leningrad. After capturing the Nevsky Pyatachok bridgehead in the Sinyavino Offensive in 1942, the division was re-designated as the 45th Guards Rifle Division. It was reformed in April 1942 from the 47th and 146th Rifle Brigades, and engaged in battles such as the Battle of Smolensk and the advance into eastern Belarus. It played a significant role in Operation Bagration where it broke through German defenses and advanced towards the Baltic in the Riga Offensive. The 70th Division participated in battles in East Prussia, including the Battle of Memel, the Battle of Königsberg and the Samland Offensive until the end of WWII. Postwar, it undertook garrison duties in Pomerania before its disbandment in early 1947.","LocalizedString":"The 252nd Rifle Regiment was a unit of the 70th Rifle Division of the Red Army during the Winter War and WWII. It was initially established in 1934 at Samara but was later moved to the Leningrad Military District. The division participated in the Winter War and received the Order of Lenin for its role in breaching the Mannerheim Line. With the outbreak of Operation Barbarossa in 1941, the division relocated and engaged in counter attacks against the German invasion at Soltsy and later defending the Neva line during the Siege of Leningrad. After capturing the Nevsky Pyatachok bridgehead in the Sinyavino Offensive in 1942, the division was re-designated as the 45th Guards Rifle Division. It was reformed in April 1942 from the 47th and 146th Rifle Brigades, and engaged in battles such as the Battle of Smolensk and the advance into eastern Belarus. It played a significant role in Operation Bagration where it broke through German defenses and advanced towards the Baltic in the Riga Offensive. The 70th Division participated in battles in East Prussia, including the Battle of Memel, the Battle of Königsberg and the Samland Offensive until the end of WWII. Postwar, it undertook garrison duties in Pomerania before its disbandment in early 1947."},"operationCost":1,"rarity":"ERarityEnum::Uncommon","cardSet":"ECardSetEnum::WinterWar","isReserved":true,"EffectType":"ECardEffectTypes::Trigger","usedTriggers":["ERegisteredCardFunction::OnOtherCardDealDamage","ERegisteredCardFunction::OnOtherCardDealDamageAddDamage"],"extraHelpTextBubbleTypes":["EHelpBubbleTypes::Veteran","EHelpBubbleTypes::Trigger"],"spawnCardName":"card_unit_252nd_RIFLES_vet","Image":{"AssetPathName":"/Game/Assets/Textures/Images/Soviet/CandidateArtwork/Winter_War/t_soviet_reinfocements.t_soviet_reinfocements","SubPathString":""},"ImageAnchor":"EImageAnchor::BotMid","artist":"Alamy Stock Photo","historyPhoto":{"AssetPathName":"/Game/Assets/Textures/HistoricalPhotos/252nd_RIFLES.252nd_RIFLES","SubPathString":""},"historyPhotoSize":{"X":512.0,"Y":320.0},"historyPhotoDescription":{"Namespace":"card_soviet","Key":"card_unit_252nd_RIFLES_photo","SourceString":"Soviet Red Army soldiers during the Siege of Leningrad, ca. 1941-43.","LocalizedString":"Soviet Red Army soldiers during the Siege of Leningrad, ca. 1941-43."},"blowUpExplosionNiagara":{"Objec